Fixed on ack-paket (uncommitted, tree commit-ready): lib/Skilletor/JSON.pm _string and _number match on $p->{s} in place (pos($p->{s}), $p->{s} =~ /\G.../gc, substr($p->{s}, ...)); no other parser path copies the text per token (_units/_fail_at copy a prefix on the error path only). Cause checked, not guessed: the per-call copy IS copy-on-write (Devel::Peek: IsCOW, COW_REFCNT 2) on both read paths. What differs is the UTF-8 flag: read_text (Encode::decode) always flags the text, utf8::decode leaves an ASCII file unflagged. A fresh copy carries no UTF-8 offset cache, so every pos() on a flagged copy converts char<->byte offsets by scanning from the start: quadratic. Same 300 KB file: unflagged 0.24 s, utf8::upgrade'd 10.74 s, read_text 10.76 s (unpatched); patched all three 0.22-0.25 s; patched with ${^UTF8CACHE}=0 a 100 KB file takes 8.9 s. Regression test t/27-state-read-large.t reads a synthetic 300778-byte sources-read.json through Skilletor::State->sources_read (bound 3 s): red unpatched 10.96 s, green patched 0.239 s. t/10-json.t green; patched js_stringify(js_parse) of the fixture is byte-identical to Node's JSON.stringify(JSON.parse). Full suite: Files=55 Tests=2736 PASS (t/65-report-json.t skips 102 conformance cases by design: no sync, check or status step to compare). k250 numbers in the handoff report to the main agent.

